---
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import Fill from '../components/Fill.astro';
import { OWNER } from '../config/legal';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Cookie policy"
  description="Which cookies B2BRated sets today, and what we will tell you before that changes."
  path="/cookies"
>
  <h2>Cookies we set today</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing is set until you choose. The first time you visit, a banner asks whether we may use Google Analytics to count
    visits. If you decline, or ignore the banner, we set no analytics cookies. If you click Accept analytics, Google
    Analytics sets its own cookies, such as one named _ga, so it can tell visits apart. The site sets no other cookies.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your choice is kept in your browser's local storage so the banner does not come back on every page. Local storage is
    not a cookie and is not sent to any server. Google may still receive basic page-view signals without cookies, as its
    consent mode allows, even when you decline.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can change your choice at any time: <button type="button" id="reset-consent" class="font-medium text-brand-800 underline">change my analytics choice</button>.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies from other companies</h2>
  <p>
    Pages load fonts, scripts and images from our own site, with one exception. The Google Tag Manager script loads from
    Google on every page. Google Analytics only sets cookies after you accept. We do not embed videos, social buttons or
    ad networks. Links to vendor websites leave this site, and those sites have their own cookie rules.
  </p>

  <h2>What will change</h2>
  <p>
    When accounts open, signing in will need a cookie that keeps you logged in. That cookie will be strictly necessary
    for the sign-in to work. If we later add advertising or other tools that use cookies, we will ask for your consent
    first, and we will update this page and the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> before either goes live.
  </p>

  <script>
    document.getElementById('reset-consent')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      try {
        localStorage.removeItem('b2b-analytics');
      } catch {}
      location.reload();
    });
  </script>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <Fill value={OWNER.email} label="contact email" />, or use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
